      <div type="clause" n="El. 18">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> El. 18</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 18" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="32" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hwa on cease<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Af_El-to-18.lnote.oe.14"/> éacniende<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Af_El-to-18.lnote.oe.15"/> wif<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#Af_El-to-18.lnote.oe.star"/> gewerde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Af_El-to-18.lnote.oe.16"/>, bete þone æwerdlan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Af_El-to-18.lnote.oe.17"/>, swa him domeras gereccen.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Af_El-to-18.lnote.oe.18"/> Gif hio<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Af_El-to-18.lnote.oe.19"/> dead<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Af_El-to-18.lnote.oe.20"/> sie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_El-to-18.lnote.oe.11"/>, selle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Af_El-to-18.lnote.oe.21"/> sawle wið sawle.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 18" corresp="#wit-g-prol-only"><pb n="32" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf hwa on ceaste eacniende wif gewyrde, gebete þone ǽwyrdlan, swa hym domeras getæcan. Gyf heo dead sy, sylle sawle wið sawle.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 18" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="33" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hwa on ceaste eacniende wif gewerde, bete þone æwyrdlan, swa him demeras gereccan. Gif heo dæd sy, sylle sawle wið sawle.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="El. 18" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="33" ed="#liebermann"/>Si rixati fuerint uiri, et percusserit quis mulierem pregnantem, et abortiuum quidem fecerit, sed ipsa uixerit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_El-to-18.lnote.oe.4"/>, subiacebit dampno, quantum expetierit maritus mulieris et arbitri iudicauerint.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_El-to-18.lnote.oe.5"/> Si autem mors eius fuerit secuta, reddat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_El-to-18.lnote.oe.6"/> animam pro anima;</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="MP 18" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="242" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Gif hwa on cease éacniende wif gewerde, bete þone æwerdlan, swa him domeras gereccen. Gif hio dead sie, selle sawle wið sawle.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="33" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn jemand bei einer Rauferei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-18.lnote.de.1"/> ein schwangeres<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-18.lnote.de.2"/> Weib<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_El-to-18.lnote.de.3"/><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#Af_El-to-18.lnote.de1.star"/> verletzt, so büsse er den Schaden, wie ihm die Richter<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_El-to-18.lnote.de.4"/> zuerkennen.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_El-to-18.lnote.de.5"/> Wenn sie todt ist, gebe er Seele<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_El-to-18.lnote.de.6"/> für Seele.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone in a brawl injures a pregnant woman, let him compensate for the damage as the judges award him. If she is dead, let him give soul for soul.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="243" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If someone in the course of a quarrel should injure a pregnant woman, let him compensate for the damage as the judges may counsel for him. If she should die, give soul for soul.</ab>
        <note type="passageSource">Exodus 21,22–23</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="33">Exodus 21.22; Exodus 21.23</note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">[21, 22] | [21, 23]</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="282"><ref target="clause:Af_9">Af 9</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="305"><ref target="clause:Af_9">Af 9</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-18.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">32</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ceast <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ceast So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-18.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">32</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-nd <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-nd So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-18.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">32</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">slea ⁊ hio <hi rend="italic">fügt zu, jedoch unterstreicht (löscht wieder) So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">slea ⁊ hio added by So, which, however, underlines it (i.e. deletes it again)</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-18.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">32</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-rd <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-rd Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-18.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">32</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">æfwyrdlan <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">æfwyrdlan Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-18.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">32</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="spaced">betæcan</hi> <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> <hi rend="spaced">getæcan</hi> <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">betæcan</hi> So; <hi rend="italic">getæcan</hi> Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-18.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">32</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">heo <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">heo Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-18.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">32</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">dæd <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">dæd So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-18.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">32</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sy <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sy Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-18.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">32</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sylle <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sylle Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-18.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">33</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">superuix. <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">superuix. Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-18.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">33</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-rit <hi rend="italic">Dm</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-rit Dm</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-18.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">33</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-det <hi rend="italic">T Vulg.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-det T Vulg.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-18.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">45</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Auch bei Abt 18 führt <hi rend="italic">ceas</hi> zu Bluttat. Dafür setzen jüngere Texte <hi rend="italic">ceast</hi> (<hi rend="italic">s.</hi> Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl.;</hi> Fries. <hi rend="italic">kase</hi>), auch Ine 35</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">In Abt 18 too <hi rend="italic">ceas</hi> leads to bloodshed. For it later texts put <hi rend="italic">ceast</hi> (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl.;</hi> Fris. <hi rend="italic">kase</hi>), also Ine 35</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-18.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">45</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Kind 1f.; Frau 3—4</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Kind 1f.; Frau 3—4</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-18.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">45</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Hs. So blieb der Bibel zuerst näher. Der Abortus in der Vulgata schien Ælfred wohl unanständig</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">MS So at first kept closer to the Bible. The abortion in the Vulgate probably seemed indecent to Ælfred</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Af_El-to-18.lnote.de1.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">33</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘schlägt und sie’ <hi rend="italic">fügt So zu</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘strikes and she’ <hi rend="italic">added by So</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-18.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">45</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Af lässt den Gatten als Ankläger und Schadentaxator fort, vielleicht um auch unvermählte Schwangere zu schützen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Af omits the husband as accuser and assessor of the damage, perhaps in order to protect unmarried pregnant women too</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-18.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">45</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ge(be)tæcan</hi> übersetzt bei Ælfred (Cosijn <hi rend="italic">Altwestsä. Gram.</hi> § 124) ‘committere, tradere’, anderwärts freilich ‘bestimmen, anordnen’; Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl.</hi> Mir scheint <hi rend="italic">gereccean</hi> (<hi rend="italic">s. Wb</hi>), das Af mehrfach von Richtern sagt, authentisch</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">ge(be)tæcan</hi> translates ‘committere, tradere’ in Ælfred (Cosijn <hi rend="italic">Altwestsä. Gram.</hi> § 124), elsewhere, it is true, ‘to determine, to ordain’; Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl.</hi> To me <hi rend="italic">gereccean</hi> (<hi rend="italic">see Wb</hi>), which Af several times uses of judges, seems authentic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-18.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">45</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Talion. Die Aufnahme des Af 9 widersprechenden Gebots kann nur bezwecken, aus göttlichem Gesetz vor Gewalttat zu warnen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Talion. The inclusion of this precept, which contradicts Af 9, can only be meant to warn against violence on the authority of divine law</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
